            "slab_cif": {
              "description": "CIF string of the surface slab structure.\nA properly formatted CIF string containing the surface slab structure on which the adsorbate will be placed. This should be a two-dimensional periodic structure with a well-defined surface and vacuum region. The slab provides the substrate for molecular adsorption.\n\"# generated using pymatgen data_Si _symmetry_space_group_name_H-M   'P 1' _cell_length_a   3.83996459 _cell_length_b   3.83996459 _cell_length_c   18.81190774 _cell_angle_alpha   90.00000000 _cell_angle_beta   90.00000000 _cell_angle_gamma   120.00000000 _symmetry_Int_Tables_number   1 _chemical_formula_structural   Si _chemical_formula_sum   Si8 _cell_volume   240.22483885 _cell_formula_units_Z   8 loop_ _symmetry_equiv_pos_site_id _symmetry_equiv_pos_as_xyz 1  'x, y, z' loop_ _atom_site_type_symbol _atom_site_label _atom_site_symmetry_multiplicity _atom_site_fract_x _atom_site_fract_y _atom_site_fract_z _atom_site_occupancy Si  Si0  1  0.83333333  0.41666667  0.10416667  1.0 Si  Si1  1  0.50000000  0.75000000  0.06250000  1.0 Si  Si2  1  0.16666667  0.08333333  0.27083333  1.0 Si  Si3  1  0.83333333  0.41666667  0.22916667  1.0 Si  Si4  1  0.50000000  0.75000000  0.43750000  1.0 Si  Si5  1  0.16666667  0.08333333  0.39583333  1.0 Si  Si6  1  0.83333333  0.41666667  0.60416667  1.0 Si  Si7  1  0.50000000  0.75000000  0.56250000  1.0 \"",
